course: dictionary
lesson: 4029
title: Names of places and people: Gaul
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Gaul is a proper name, so it starts with a capital letter. It is the old name for a large area of western Europe, the land the Romans knew as Gaul. Mostly it is where France and Belgium are today.
explain: «Julius Caesar, a brilliant general, conquered Gaul, today's France, took power in Rome.» The words today's France are your clue. Gaul is an old name for land we now call France. Try it: swap in France and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Gaul can also name people. A Gaul was a person from Gaul, one of the Celtic peoples who lived there. Look for small clues like «the Gauls» and «Gaulish» to tell you whether the word means the place or the people.
fact: Gaul is a proper name, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: Gaul was the old Roman name for a large area of western Europe, mostly France and Belgium today.
fact: A Gaul was a person from Gaul, one of the Celtic peoples who lived there.
fact: «Gaulish» describes things that belong to Gaul or its people, like a Gaulish village.
fact: Julius Caesar, a Roman general, conquered Gaul. He was killed in 44 BC by senators who feared he wanted to be king.
exercise: What was Gaul? | A kind of Roman boat | A Roman general's name | A city in Italy ruled by kings | *An old name for a large area of western Europe, mostly France and Belgium today
exercise: «Julius Caesar conquered Gaul.» Who were the Gauls? | Animals that lived in the French countryside | *People from Gaul, Celtic peoples who lived there | Roman soldiers who marched to Gaul | Senators in Rome
exercise: In the sentence «Julius Caesar, a brilliant general, conquered Gaul, today's France», what does today's France tell you? | *Gaul is an old name for the land we now call France | Caesar was French | Gaul is a city near Paris | Gaul is a river in Italy
test: Which word means something that belongs to Gaul or its people? | Celtic | Senator | *Gaulish | Roman
test: According to the sentence, in which year was Julius Caesar killed by senators? | 100 AD | 2000 BC | 1066 | *44 BC
exam: Why does Gaul start with a capital letter? | Because it is a very important word | Because it is the first word of a sentence | Because it is a Roman number | *Because it is a proper name for a place
